WEBVTT

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.620
"RE: Program Segment Ideas
Message: Live broadcast every week
from a listener's house"

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:19.750
"Koya Ishida
RE: Program Segment Ideas
Message: Have Minare comment
on your future dreams"

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.870
"Your future dreams"

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.370
"Your future dreams"
Future...

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.790
"Dreams"

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.160
"Dreams"
Dreams?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.250
My seminar wasn't enough to discourage you
from wanting to become an AD at a radio station?

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:37.790
Not at all. Can you give me advice
on how to become an AD in radio?

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.790
But why an AD?

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.910
Um, well, actually...

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.950
I'm more of a behind-the-scenes
kind of person in nature.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.450
I can't come up with any offbeat ideas, either.

00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:51.000
But I love radio, so I want to
take part in it any way I can.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:54.450
Well, I'll tell you this...

00:00:54.450 --> 00:01:01.370
No radio station would hire someone who's
only interested in being an assistant director.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.040
The ideal assistant director would think...

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:06.910
"When I become a producer,

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:12.870
I'll stop this boring program and double
the ratings with an eye-opening segment!"

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:18.200
Being motivated by some shameless
fantasy like that is just right.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.910
Anaguma-Hunting Prohibited.

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:32.290
As planned, we'll feature the in-studio
appearance of Joker Skonsky for this broadcast.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.950
That means we finally get
to put a face on that name.

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.500
Let's hope it's a high-school girl.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.410
How many times do you have to say that?

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:41.910
But it's impressive. We used their content three
weeks in a row since their first submission.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.700
Their writing is comparable
to writers around here, too.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.370
Why don't we hire them to write our jokes?

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:50.250
Mr. Nishiki, Mr. Anaguma, Joker Skonsky is here.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.250
All right. Let them in.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.500
Come on in.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.700
Oh?

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.450
Seriously?

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:03.450
I was fully expecting a dude even though
I said I hope it's a high-school girl.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.830
I'm Tachibana.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:07.910
Please don't be too hard on me today.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.750
"Episode 12: I Want to Convey It to You"
Ten minutes until you're on.

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.870
"Episode 12: I Want to Convey It to You"
All righty.

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:50.370
So how many submissions
did we receive, after all?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.000
We received 80 from the website
and 30 from Miss Minare's Twitter.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.450
Not bad for an up-and-coming program.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:03.080
Re-uploading the video of Miss Minare
storming into the studio was quite effective.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.750
These were all submitted just now.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.580
I checked the ones I think
we might be able to use.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.580
Okay.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:16.950
The submissions being presented today...
Were any of them written by you, Mr. Kureko?

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.330
Or were they all?

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.080
I thought of writing some just in case,

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:22.790
but surprisingly, there were
quite a few good submissions.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:25.120
None of them were written by me.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.620
Guess there are a lot of bored people out there.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.580
There must be lots of listeners

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:35.450
who are quietly hoping to see a Hokkaido-native
amateur become a big-name celebrity.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:39.910
In other words, they're anticipating me becoming
a Yo Oizumi-level big-name celebrity, huh?

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.330
Well, there've been plenty
of failed cases so far.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.250
So, what about the script this time?

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.200
There isn't one.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.950
As long as you have time,
read the listeners' submissions,

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:52.750
comment on them, and at the end
reveal the one you deem best.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:55.910
I'll scan through the ones that get
submitted during the broadcast,

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:58.580
but you're in charge of the ones
that get submitted via Twitter.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.830
So I need to keep checking
while I'm live on-air.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.290
It's so radio-like.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.450
Because it is radio.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:09.750
Doing a classic segment like this on your
program actually seems like a curve ball to me.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.910
You say that,

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:15.450
but maybe you're just being sentimental
right now since you're leaving radio.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.450
Hmm...

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:22.330
Then that means... I must be
reluctant to leave this world...

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.910
Mr. Kureko...

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:30.000
So that's how you mislead young women,
acting like you're some action hero movie actor.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.200
Get your mind out of the gutter.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.200
Did something happen with Komoto?

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.330
What? Um, I don't know...

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.040
What about Mr. Komoto?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.290
I don't know what spurred him to do this.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.500
But he said he wanted to record
real sounds of the wind,

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.330
so he's at the summit of Mt. Moiwa right now.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:46.000
At this hour?!

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:55.660
Chuya.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:57.620
Where is Miss Makie tonight?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.080
She said she had something to do
and left the restaurant early at 10:30 PM.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.500
Haven't heard from her since...

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.450
Haven't heard from her?
It's almost 3 AM right now.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:09.120
I'm sure she'll be back soon. If she doesn't get
to bed soon, it'll be tough working tomorrow--

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.080
That's beside the point!
Why the hell haven't you called her yet?

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.910
Ah. Well, yeah. I called her just now
but she didn't pick up.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:17.540
The more reason to be concerned!

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:19.500
Go look for her!

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:24.540
Now that she mentioned it, it is way too late.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.160
But where am I supposed to go search anyway?

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.750
Yes?

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.160
Ah, what a relief. I was worried
because it's really late now.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.410
Where are you right now?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:40.660
Yeah. Huh? You're that close?

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.290
I'm sorry for not checking in.

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:56.080
It's fine. As long as you're okay.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.040
It's not good for a woman to be alone
in the park at night though.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.000
Ah... I was just celebrating by myself.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.450
Oh, yeah? For what?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.700
I was so nervous today...

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.620
Um... I promise to tell you
about it another day.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.080
Oh, okay.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.120
All right, then.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.750
Mr. Nakahara.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:24.830
Hm?

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:26.250
I...

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.750
I'm actually really scared right now.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.660
And really nervous.

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:38.290
This is the first time I've decided on things
for myself without consulting my brother.

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:44.830
I might make a lot of wrong choices...

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.370
I may create enemies...

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.540
But...

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:54.410
No matter how much I fail,
I want you to be there

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.250
until the end, Mr. Nakahara.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:05.120
I promise to return your generosity eventually.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:13.200
"You've always sought after
a source of power outside yourself.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:17.500
But it's actually something
that exists within you.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:20.200
It only exists within you."

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:23.950
That's from the late-night drama,
<i>Wild Journey Hizageruge</i>.

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:27.450
What? I thought those were
the words of Freud's daughter.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:30.160
Sorry... That's probably what
the line's based off.

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:37.120
Eventually, I'm planning on leaving
Voyager to start my own restaurant.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:41.120
So Miss Tachibana,
if you find yourself in a bind

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.790
after making too many
wrong choices in the future,

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:46.200
you can always help out
at my restaurant if you want.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.120
I'll pay you a salary this time, too.

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:55.540
Hey...! What...?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:58.200
You... You're always...

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.200
You're always saying things like that
out of the kindness of your heart.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.080
It... It always gets me...

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.200
I can't stand it...

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.450
Um... Sorry!

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:11.910
But I don't know what part of that
conversation would make you cry.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.700
Sixty seconds until you're on.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:15.830
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:17.790
You left everything to me from the start.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.750
And isn't the broadcast writer supposed to stay
in the booth with me while I'm on air?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:26.080
With you... it's better to be
a spectator than an accomplice.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.700
Then if I say something funny, you better
laugh out loud, louder than anybody.

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:32.660
That's all on you.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.830
Bring it on.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.290
Ten seconds...

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:39.790
Seven... six... five seconds...

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:59.660
It's time for Minare Koda's Wave, Listen to Me!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.080
Those who went off to perform
<i>ushi no koku mairi </i>and curse someone

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:03.620
by stabbing a long nail into a straw doll

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:06.290
must be back unwinding by now at 3:30 AM.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:09.950
Just in time for Minare Koda's
Wave, Listen to Me!

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:15.160
Tonight we're broadcasting live from Moiwayama
Radio like an ordinary program for once.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:17.000
And why, you ask?

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.330
Yes! As you all know,

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:22.660
I'll be revealing the new segment idea
I've selected from everyone's submissions!

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:23.910
Don't get me wrong.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.040
I won't recklessly broadcast live some
controversial idea just because I can.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:29.290
I'm not trying to make this an extreme program
that stirs up the internet like that.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:32.620
For those who didn't know about this, we're
still accepting ideas during the broadcast.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.410
Your ideas may still make it on air.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:38.040
Please submit them on
the program's website or on Twitter.

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.790
Now let's get started!

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:41.950
First off, this one's from radio name Onami.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:44.080
"What do you think of 'Radio Relay'?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.370
You'll give us a quiz that'll reveal
a location. Then the first listener

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:53.500
who figures it out will meet you there
at the place to start a radio drama.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:57.910
The listener must show up with
a script they've written beforehand

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:01.750
and you're forced to
act it out then and there.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:07.000
So with impromptu acting the listener
has full control of what drama will unfold."

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.330
I see...

00:11:08.330 --> 00:11:11.790
Hey, this is a total trap!
It's way too complicated, too.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:15.370
Remember when I first spoke on the radio?!

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.450
That was a total trap!

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:20.540
What if someone intends to mess with me?

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:25.290
Well, I wouldn't mind if someone like
Furiwake-oyakata showed up... Oh... Whoa!

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.620
Moving on to the next submission...

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:32.120
Huh?

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.500
