00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.250
The time is 3:50 AM.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:55.080
Normally, it's time for Sound High Tide,

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:57.750
but this program has been extended
due to the circumstances.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:00.450
What, seriously? Is it okay
for me to keep doing this?

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.910
Nanba, I'll deliver the script to her.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.040
What? Oh, okay...

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.370
The power's out.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.950
Mr. Nakahara, let's head to Voyager.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.910
What? Why would we go to the restaurant?

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.790
I don't know what's going to happen
to critical infrastructure,

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:18.790
but if the power outage continues and
distribution halts, the least we could do is...

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.040
A soup kitchen?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:21.000
Yes.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:26.040
You're right. Voyager has lots of supplies. I'll
check with Manager to see if we could use them.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.040
I shouldn't be on air any longer.

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:32.330
A professional announcer should be
talking during an emergency like this.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:34.500
We just received new information.

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:39.080
The epicenter is the southern part of Iburi,
Hokkaido. The hypocenter is 45km deep.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.540
The magnitude of the quake is...

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.500
"Quit acting like an amateur"

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:48.290
"Quit acting like an amateur"
...estimated to be 6.8...

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:53.830
The tide levels may be affected by this quake,

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.200
"Normally it would feel a bit
cruel to expect a newcomer like you
to handle this during an emergency."
but there is no concern for a tsunami.

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.080
"But you've got bigger balls than that, right?"

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.910
Agh! All right!

00:15:12.910 --> 00:15:16.410
Now here's a message from radio name
Yumenyan of Kushiro!

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:20.830
"We lost power here at our place in the city, so
we're listening to this program in candlelight.

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:25.410
Fellow Hokkaidoans! Let's help each other out
and get through this crisis together!"

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:27.870
Thank you Yumenyan for your powerful message!

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:28.330
--Speaking of Kushiro, that's where my
parents live. I wonder how they're doing.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.120
--Couldn't you think of a better
radio name, Yumenyan?
--Speaking of Kushiro, that's where my
parents live. I wonder how they're doing.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.790
--Couldn't you think of a better
radio name, Yumenyan?
--I can't wait to hear from more people
in other parts of Hokkaido!

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:37.580
Oh, we've received another one
from radio name Asahikawa Smile.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:41.000
"The power had gone out, it was
all dark and I was sad and lonely.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.410
But as soon as I turned on the radio,
I felt relief hearing another person's voice."

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:47.040
Thank you for sharing that, it makes me happy.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:50.200
It's true, anyone would feel anxious
being alone in a situation like this.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:53.540
I would be glad if I could be of any help.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:54.040
--Next is from radio name Dateotoko of Hakodate.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:56.200
--Manager isn't picking up.
--Next is from radio name Dateotoko of Hakodate.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:16:00.950
--Calls won't go through, the traffic
lights and streetlights are down...
--"After the quake, the power went out so I
couldn't turn on the TV or check the internet.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.290
--I've never experienced Sapporo
like this before.
--But I'm touched to be able
to listen to the radio!"

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:12.040
--Nice, now that's Hokkaido's
prized local convenience store.
--There are lots of people out there
who can't tune into the radio, either.

00:16:12.040 --> 00:16:13.700
If you are listening to this program right now,

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.120
please pass on the information
to your neighbors and friends.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.660
There're three days' worth
of food in the fridge.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:22.620
The freezer's fully stocked with the perfect
ingredients for a soup kitchen.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.750
You mean Gagarin's soup curry?

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:25.950
Eek!

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:26.830
Manager?!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.000
Brother?!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.660
What are you two doing together?

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:34.330
Mr. Toru wanted my advice
on his younger sister's future.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.660
Well, I couldn't refuse his invitation...

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:41.500
But this is perfect. Could we please use
Gagarin's curry for the soup kitchen?

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:46.120
I can't bear the idea of keeping it
in my freezer any longer!

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:51.200
If it can help in an emergency like this,
I'm sure Master at Gagarin would be happy.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.500
It'll help immensely!

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:54.410
I'll begin the preparations now.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.450
But what are you going to do about the fire?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:58.910
I found a gas cylinder in storage.

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:00.450
There're disposable to-go containers, too,

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.950
so we'll be able to pass out
the curry on the street.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.500
"Impressive..."
so we'll be able to pass out
the curry on the street.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:05.000
And one more thing, Manager...

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.080
Huh?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.080
The three-days' worth of ingredients
in the fridge...

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:11.250
They might spoil during this power outage.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.830
So... Um...

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.830
Of course! Feel free to use it all up.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.450
Thank you very much.

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.450
Moving on with a submission from
radio name Furudanuki from Susukino!

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.910
"I've been serving as a Manager of
a <i>soapland </i>for over 30 years here.

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:29.200
I think this is the time to give back to my
community. Do you have any suggestions?"

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:34.660
Let's see. There might be some people
who won't be able to take baths tonight.

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.250
So how about you operate as a public bath today?

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:41.700
Plus, those who are curious could come
check it out and return as customers later?

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.450
Yes?

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.200
How is it?

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:53.370
I just got here.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:57.330
Sorry for making you, a mixer, do this.

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:01.660
Unlike the other relay stations, there are
no power generators in Kitami and Toya.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:02.830
I don't mind.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:05.500
This is part of "Don't stop the signal."

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.410
You're a great help.

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.450
After Toya, I'll head to Kitami.

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:12.200
Whoa... Kitami is a bit far from there...

00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:14.580
Moving on with radio name CS.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.330
"After the quake, the convenience store
I work at was jammed

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.040
--with heavier traffic than expected,
with long lines at the register.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.660
--You made it.
--with heavier traffic than expected,
with long lines at the register.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.160
--I only followed orders.
--with heavier traffic than expected,
with long lines at the register.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.290
--"During an emergency, rush to
the station no matter what," right?
--A customer who purchased two bottles
of water handed me one of them and said

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.790
--Well, now that you're here.
Could we have you switch with Minare?
--that it was for me."

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.040
--Well, now that you're here.
Could we have you switch with Minare?
--That made me so happy,
I almost burst into tears!"

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.080
--Of course. That's why I came.
--That made me so happy,
I almost burst into tears!"

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:31.750
--Of course. That's why I came.
--Wow, what a touching story.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.250
It almost made me cry, too!

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.000
"We're switching for the 5 AM news report."

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.250
So... All right!

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:44.290
The extended broadcast of Minare Koda's
Wave, Listen to Me! has now come to an end.

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:47.700
Thank you everyone for all
the messages during this difficult time!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:50.200
I'm gonna go check on the crops...
Just kidding...

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:54.330
I'm gonna go check in on
my neighbors, too. See ya!

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:58.950
♪ MRS... JOZV FM... ♪

00:18:58.950 --> 00:18:59.790
Good job.

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:02.120
--Ah... Oh, yeah, thank you.
--Moiwayama Radio.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:06.160
--Despite the disaster, your talk made me laugh.
--Moiwayama Radio brings you
the 5 AM news report.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.160
Oh, um... Thank you.

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:18.750
Madoka Chishiro's September Blue Moon.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:24.750
We're broadcasting a little earlier
with different content than usual today.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.660
First off, updates on the earthquake.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.870
At around 3:32 AM in Hokkaido,

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:33.370
a strong earthquake with a maximum
intensity of 6 occurred.

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.200
--Miss Minare, you were a trooper!
--Currently, there is a widespread
power outage all over Hokkaido.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:37.660
--Yeah, I'm spent.
--Currently, there is a widespread
power outage all over Hokkaido.

00:19:37.660 --> 00:19:40.200
Forgive me if I'm being unscrupulous
at a time like this,

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.450
but the first thought that came up
after Sapporo went dark was...

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.830
"The stars are beautiful."

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:50.120
I'm sure many of you are looking up
at the stars right now, too.

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:53.950
And I think a few of you
probably hummed this tune.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.910
Now let's give it a listen.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:24.080
<i>Look up at the stars in the night sky</i>

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:34.790
<i>The tiny lights from the tiny stars</i>

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:47.080
<i>Are singing of a small happiness</i>

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:52.500
<i>Let's hold each other's hands</i>

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:58.040
<i>Let's chase after our dreams</i>

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:08.750
<i>Together, it won't be a struggle at all</i>

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:19.540
<i>Look up at the stars in the sky</i>

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:30.290
<i>A nameless star like us</i>

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:40.290
<i>Is praying for a small happiness</i>

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:50.450
Now that's a professional.

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:52.870
During a disaster,
there's nothing more comforting

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:55.250
than hearing a regular
personality's familiar voice.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:56.790
Mr. Mato!

00:21:56.790 --> 00:21:58.120
Thank you for today.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:21:59.450
All right!

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:01.250
You're not going on break?

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:03.830
Not while Chishiro's on air.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.250
Um...

00:22:06.250 --> 00:22:08.950
Mr. Kureko, even if you become a novelist,

00:22:08.950 --> 00:22:13.200
when I make my debut as a director,
can I ask you to write the script?

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:14.830
You're asking me now?

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:17.000
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:22:19.580 --> 00:22:23.200
Well, if it sounds interesting enough.

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:24.870
I'm going to make it happen, no matter what!

00:22:24.870 --> 00:22:27.080
Minare, you're free to go home now.

00:22:27.080 --> 00:22:28.290
Don't you work today?

00:22:28.290 --> 00:22:29.290
Work?

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:31.200
Ah, you mean at Voyager.

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:33.330
I wonder if they're going to be open today.

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:36.250
I don't know. I guess I'll have to ask Manager.

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:38.950
But to be honest, I'd rather be
here at the station right now...

00:22:38.950 --> 00:22:39.700
Oh...

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:44.160
But are you sure? A once-a-week,
dead-of-night 20-minute radio program--

00:22:44.160 --> 00:22:46.830
is that really your final abode?

00:22:46.830 --> 00:22:49.700
Is this a solicitation for
a self-development seminar?

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:52.250
The restaurant's probably closed
because of the power outage.

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.160
I'll come back after I get some fresh air.

00:22:55.160 --> 00:22:59.080
I always wanted to sleep in
that prison of a napping room.

00:23:07.790 --> 00:23:12.330
I thought radio was on its way to extinction...

00:23:12.330 --> 00:23:15.160
But it's actually pretty great.

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:20.330
Mr. Mato dragged me into this,
but now I've made my resolve.

00:23:20.330 --> 00:23:23.450
I'll be the one dragging Mr. Mato
and others into this from here on out.

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:28.160
No, Sapporo! No, Hokkaido! No, all of Japan!

00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:29.620
Miss Minare!

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:33.830
We're doing a soup kitchen at Voyager!

00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:37.290
We're here to pick you up since we
wanted your help, too, Miss Minare!

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:41.870
Ah, when I've just declared that I'm
devoting myself to radio now..

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:42.910
Well...

00:23:42.910 --> 00:23:45.450
I won't be able to support myself
just doing that.

00:23:46.830 --> 00:23:48.620
All right, let's go!

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:52.580
I'll pick up everyone's voices from town
and use it as content for the radio!

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.870
"Thank you for watching!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
